    <string name="capture_hear_title">What can TrailMix hear?</string>
    <string name="capture_hear_body">Microphone: always works. In-person conversation, speakerphone, anything the mic can hear.\n\nPhone audio (opt-in in Recording options): works for most apps, such as browsers, podcasts, games and most video players.\n\nWhat can\'t be captured:\n• YouTube and DRM or streaming apps. They opt out of capture, and Android enforces it.\n• The other side of phone and VoIP calls. Android never shares call audio with any app.\n\nFor those, put the call or video on speakerphone and let the mic pick it up.\n\nTrailMix can\'t tell up front whether an app allows capture. If phone audio stays silent, a hint appears on this screen.</string>
    <string name="capture_projection_title">Hear what your phone plays</string>
    <string name="capture_projection_body">To transcribe meetings and videos, TrailMix can listen to the audio other apps play.\n\nAndroid only grants that through its screen-share permission, so the next dialog will mention your screen. TrailMix only receives the audio stream. It never records, stores or sees your screen.\n\nAndroid blocks every app from hearing protected voice-call audio, and some apps opt out of capture entirely.</string>
    <string name="capture_projection_continue">Continue</string>
    <string name="capture_projection_not_now">Not now</string>
